## 11 — Testing examples (use these to test your agent in AI Studio)

Paste each test case into the Input collection step or provide as a single JSON input to the planner. Expected behaviour described after each case.

### Test 1 — Simple single-subject short window

**Input:**

```json
{
  "exam_date": "2025-12-01",
  "subjects": {"Maths": ["Algebra ch1","Algebra ch2","Geometry ch1"]},
  "hours_per_day": 2,
  "weak_subjects": ["Maths"],
  "session_length": 45,
  "days_off": []
}
```

**Expected:** Plan spreads 3 chapters across remaining days, gives extra sessions to Maths (because weak), includes short daily checklists.

### Test 2 — Multiple subjects, fixed days off

**Input:**

```json
{
  "exam_date": "2025-12-10",
  "subjects": {"Physics": ["Ch1","Ch2","Ch3"], "Chemistry": ["Ch1","Ch2"]},
  "hours_per_day": 3,
  "weak_subjects": ["Physics"],
  "session_length": 50,
  "days_off": ["2025-11-22","2025-11-29"]
}
```

**Expected:** Schedules account for days_off, gives more Physics sessions, schedules two revision cycles.

### Test 3 — Many chapters, low hours (should advise)

**Input:**

```json
{
  "exam_date": "2025-11-30",
  "subjects": {"Biology": ["Ch1","Ch2","Ch3","Ch4","Ch5","Ch6","Ch7","Ch8"]},
  "hours_per_day": 1,
  "weak_subjects": [],
  "session_length": 45,
  "days_off": []
}
```

**Expected:** Agent should detect insufficient time and propose increasing hours or removing days_off. If forced, it should still allocate but mark it as "risky".

### Test 4 — Realistic student (3 subjects)

**Input:**

```json
{
  "exam_date": "2025-12-05",
  "subjects": {"Maths": ["Alg(8)","Geo(6)"], "English": ["Grammar","Poetry"], "CS": ["Ch1","Ch2","Ch3"]},
  "hours_per_day": 4,
  "weak_subjects": ["Maths"],
  "session_length": 50,
  "days_off": ["2025-11-28"]
}
```

**Expected:** Full plan with ~4 hours/day blocks, spaced breaks, revision cycles, and daily checklists.

### Test 5 — Custom session length

**Input:** session_length = 30 — agent should create shorter blocks and increase number per day.

### Test 6 — Late start (few days)

**Input:** exam_date is 7 days away and many topics — should prioritize highest weight chapters and recommend urgent plan.

### Test 7 — No weak subjects

**Input:** no weak_subjects — allocate evenly.

### Test 8 — Weekend-only study plan

**Input:** hours_per_day set but days_off configured so only weekends remain — agent should allocate heavier sessions to weekends and warn about long sessions.

